      "writtenOn": "2024-01-11T01:03:33Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why is this called write? Is it referring to ioctl opcodes using the _IOW macro? If so how do you avoid collisions with the write operation in drivers that also need to implement the write operation in file_operations.\n\n(edit) It looks like these names are local to this driver, but I still think they should be renamed to avoid unnecessary confusion",
      "revId": "8cb9ad5d5cf5cd989d82dff8e0112dbeb0976532",
